"""A paper using a CTAN bibliography style not in the Tectonic bundle.

Demonstrates `ctan_packages = ["biblatex-apa"]` to pull a modern APA
citation style (post-2022) and compose it with `biber = True`. Real
modern biblatex extension styles depend on biblatex 3.18+ / biber
2.18+, which is *newer than the bundle ships* (3.17 / 2.17). The
example workspace opts into the modern-biblatex toolchain overlay
via `tectonic.toolchain(modern_biblatex = True)` in
`examples/MODULE.bazel`, which fetches biblatex 3.21 + biber 2.21
and overlays them so this works. See DESIGN.md §5 item #12 and
docs/site/getting-started/ctan-packages.md "Modern biblatex".

Workspaces *without* the opt-in stick with the bundle's pinned
3.17/2.17 stack — fine for most documents (the bundle ships the
five core biblatex styles), but biblatex-apa / -chicago / -ieee /
-nature etc. need the overlay.
"""

load("@rules_latex//latex:defs.bzl", "latex_document", "latex_test")

latex_document(
    name = "ctan_paper",
    srcs = [
        "paper.tex",
        "references.bib",
    ],
    biber = True,
    ctan_packages = ["biblatex-apa"],
    main = "paper.tex",
    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
)

latex_test(
    name = "ctan_paper_compiles",
    srcs = [
        "paper.tex",
        "references.bib",
    ],
    biber = True,
    ctan_packages = ["biblatex-apa"],
    main = "paper.tex",
    # Confirms biblatex-apa actually loaded (not just silently
    # falling back to a default style).
    required_patterns = ["apa"],
)
